In classic WoW, warlocks favor voidwalkers over succubi for questing and leveling primarily due to **Consume Shadows** and **Sacrifice**. 

- **Consume Shadows** passively restores the voidwalker's health out of combat, drastically reducing downtime for resummoning and healing during solo questing.  
- **Sacrifice** allows the warlock to instantly transfer all damage taken to the voidwalker, acting as a "panic button" against elite mobs or ambushes—critical for survivability when questing alone.  

While the succubus offers superior utility (Invisibility, CC, and threat reduction via Soothing Kiss), its lack of self-healing and damage mitigation makes it less durable for solo play. Voidwalkers provide reliable tanking and minimal maintenance, letting warlocks focus on questing without constant resummoning or health management. [end of text]


